<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kulin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kulin nation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kulin are an alliance of five Aboriginal nations of central Victoria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, including the Wurundjeri and Boonwurrung, whose lands cover the Port Phillip region. They share related languages and kinship ties. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a> was founded on Kulin land in 1835, and colonisation rapidly dispossessed them; the Coranderrk station near Healesville became a centre of their community and political action.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kulin.jpg" alt="Kulin" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nick carson at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kulin_Map.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
